easoning_effort. That seed fills only the dimensions omitted at the\\n  callsite, an explicit flag always wins per dimension, and the seeded pair\\n  still passes the ordinary ceiling, so a default can never widen a bound. A\\n  role with no configured default keeps explicit selection mandatory. Inspect\\n  what a role resolves to before spawning with:\\n    task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER)'\\n  Inspect the current registry with: task-board q 'models(agent=codex)'\\n\\n  With model_criterion less_or_equal or greater_or_equal, every spawn also\\n  requires --selection-rationale with one non-empty line explaining the chosen\\n  pair. If policy changes the requested pair, spawn records the requested-pair\\n  rationale tuple in task notes, creates no run, and reports requested ->\\n  resolved. Re-evaluate the resolved pair, then either re-request within\\n  bounds/escalate or re-invoke with --ack-resolved <model>/<effort> matching it\\n  exactly and fresh rationale text. After whitespace normalization that text\\n  must differ byte-for-byte from every rationale already recorded for the task\\n  and role. Pass-through ordered selections do not use --ack-resolved.\\n  model_criterion equal uses neither flag and forbids selection assessments.\\n\\n  spawn-policy-v3 uses the admitted (model, effort) pair set as the sole\\n  admission authority; allowed_models and entries are two mutually exclusive\\n  input forms that both translate into it, and neither is itself the\\n  authority. spawn-policy-v4 is the identical wire shape under a new\\n  contract_version spelling -- the version v2 migration guidance now targets --\\n  and everything below applies to it unchanged.\\n  PolicyRank, registry order, lifecycle, and recommendation never change that\\n  set; an ordered entry consults capability rank only against an\\n  operator-approved entries_expansion_digest. An out-of-set model is refused, or resolved to the exact configured\\n  resolution_model. adjustment_confirmation=required uses the rationale/ack\\n  boundary above; none forbids both flags. Inspect the target-effective policy\\n  with project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER).\\n  Grandfathered v2 ordered and effort-only policies use the frozen compatibility\\n  snapshot. Their project_config migration objects are read-only; task-board\\n  never rewrites repository config automatically.\\n\\n  Optimize maximum task quality per token: assess scope, complexity, risk,\\n  required autonomy, validation burden, and expected context and token cost before launch.\\n  For board-managed Codex work, max is the highest recommended effort. ultra\\n  remains compatible on supported models but adds model-internal delegation;\\n  prefer task-board roles, RUN lifecycle, dependencies, and reviewer routing\\n  for predictable delegation.\\n\\nWorkload-aware recommendations:\\n  When spawn.workload_classes is configured, first query the target\\n  spawn-preflight with task_class=... or workload_class=.... Reason from the\\n  returned available pairs, ranking, provenance, dropped reasons, and snapshot.\\n  Then explicitly spawn with exactly one of --workload-task-class or\\n  --workload-class, plus the exact --recommendation-snapshot-digest and one\\n  non-empty --recommendation-rationale line. The selected available pair may\\n  follow or consciously reject the ranking. A recommendation never supplies a\\n  missing model/effort, widens authority, or auto-selects a pair.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  # Queue a Codex run with an explicit model and reasoning choice\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max\\n\\n  # Workload-aware explicit selection after a matching spawn-preflight query\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-luna --reasoning-effort high --workload-task-class code --recommendation-snapshot-digest sha256:... --recommendation-rationale \\\"Bounded implementation; Luna retains every validation gate\\\"\\n\\n  # Validate instruction resource is linked before spawning\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max --instruction impl-guide.md\\n\\n  # Spawn with specific model and budget\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent claude --model claude-opus-5 --budget 5.0 \\\\\\n    --instruction impl-guide.md\\n\\n  # Queue a balanced Codex model with an explicit effort\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-terra --reasoning-effort max\\n===WORKTREE HELP===\\nInspect and repair the Story-scoped Git workspaces that repository-mutating\\nspawns run in.\\n\\nEach Story gets one managed worktree under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on a\\nshort-lived task-board/story/<STORY-ID> branch forked from trunk. Trunk is\\nspawn.worktree_isolation.integration_base_branch when configured, and otherwise\\nresolves from refs/remotes/origin/HEAD and then the current branch.\\n\\nThese commands require a local authoritative board. On a remote board they\\nrefuse with worktree_isolation_requires_local_board and do nothing else.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board worktree [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  abort                 Stop using a Story workspace, preserving its work by default\\n  checkpoint            Commit an accepted leaf onto its Story branch while preserving integrating\\n  close-landed          Close an element whose accepted candidate is already on the protected trunk\\n  complete              Prove an accepted Story's code landed on its own repository, then record its board state in the board repository\\n  converge              Refresh a pinned Story workspace onto fresh trunk, carrying its uncommitted delta\\n  gc                    Release Story leases whose holding runs are provably terminal\\n  integrate             Land an accepted Story candidate on trunk and commit its board state\\n  integrating           Classify every element parked at integrating: awaiting a landing, board-only, already on trunk, or deferred\\n  invalidate-acceptance Release an invalidated or failed-revalidation acceptance back to rework\\n  obligations           List Change Request revisions that no live run owns\\n  prepare-landed-review Export a signed current-default tree for a new producer handoff and exact-tree review\\n  reconcile-trunk       Move the control root's trunk onto fresh protected authority when every local commit is already delivered there\\n  refresh-candidate     Refresh an initial or rework candidate base without losing uncommitted files\\n  repair                Re-materialize a recorded workspace whose worktree is missing\\n  start-landed-rework   Reprove a landed-review export and durably authorize normal producer rework\\n  status                Report managed Story workspaces and what blocks their cleanup\\n  transaction           Inspect and dispose of a refused or abandoned integration transaction\\n  trunk-rewrite         Report and migrate Story workspaces orphaned by a rewrite of protected trunk history\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for worktree\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board worktree [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n===HANDOFF HELP===\\nResolve the configured role end status, verify every checklist item and\\nat least one stored task-scoped outcome resource, and apply the ordinary\\ncascading status transition under one mutation lock.\\n\\nThe command fails closed with all missing evidence and does not change status.\\nAttach or update the outcome with the resource or mutation CLI before handoff.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board handoff <ELEMENT-ID> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --commit-ack string   Mover acknowledgement for an enforced done transition\\n      --format string       Output format: compact or json (default \\\"compact\\\")\\n  -h, --help                help for handoff\\n      --role string         Role whose configured end_status must be applied\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 12033,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3009,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
